	quest.563FC8788BBCE015.quest_desc: [
		"&l&2【Backstory】&l&6Prologue&r"
		"&d&lChapter I The Dragon Race"
		"&7        In ancient times, the dragon race was once prosperous, becoming the rulers of the Minecraft world. Vast expanses of land were covered by forests, the home of the Forest Dragon; active crustal movements formed numerous underground caves, the home of the Cave Dragon; beyond the land stretched endless oceans, the home of the Sea Dragon; in the boundless heights of the firmament, the Aether Dragon soared freely; on the polar ice caps, the Tundra Dragon hunted silently. Back then, humans, like all other races in the world, struggled to survive under the oppression of the dragons."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&d&lChapter II The First Fire Receiver"
		"&7         In ancient times, human survival was difficult. Humans sent a brave one to seek cooperation with the dragons. Undeterred by danger, this brave one ventured deep into various dragon lairs, teetering on the edge of life and death countless times. Eventually, the progenitor of the Cave Dragons took an interest in him. The arrogant dragons looked down upon the ant-like human before them, finding it merely amusing, but considering his perseverance, they ultimately agreed to sign a pact with humanity. The pact stipulated that the dragons would teach humans magic, but the price was that humans must become slaves to the dragons and never rebel. The Fire Receiver learned magic from the Cave Dragon progenitor, bringing light to humanity, and was later revered as the 'First Fire Receiver.'"
		"&7         The First Fire Receiver was exceptionally gifted, inventing other types of magic from the art of flame. These derivative magics later formed the major schools. From then on, humanity gained the power to contend with the dragons."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&d&lChapter III The Thousand-Year War"
		"&7        A century later, humanity developed city-states of various sizes and gradually grew unwilling to remain slaves to the dragons. The aging Fire Receiver, uniting with humanity's great mages, unilaterally tore up the pact and declared war on the dragons. No one expected this war to last a thousand years. For a millennium, dragons bled, mages fell, the ground was littered with corpses, the oceans ran red with blood, and heaven and earth changed color. Later generations called this conflict the 'Thousand-Year War.'"
		"&7        Though dragons were born powerful, they reproduced with difficulty; humans, however, sprang up like bamboo shoots after rain, endlessly propagating. Ultimately, at the cost of countless great mages, humanity summoned the masters of each magical school and defeated the ruler of the dragons—the Dragon King. Yet, the Dragon King was too powerful; his body and soul were difficult to destroy. So, humanity used magic to tear open dimensional rifts, sealing the Dragon King's remains in another world. Thus, the thousand-year-long war came to an end. To commemorate the war's end, humanity named the other world where the Dragon King was sealed 'The End,' and called the Dragon King the 'Ender Dragon.' After the Ender Dragon was sealed, the dragon race gradually declined, hiding away in remote lands, and humanity replaced them as the new rulers of the Minecraft continent."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&d&lChapter IV The Sealing"
		"&7        Humanity used the world's hardest bedrock and obsidian to build the End Altar, and created ten obsidian pillars to suppress it. The dimensional rift leading to The End was also sealed, requiring 12 Eyes of Ender to activate the End Portal. Humanity also built underground military fortresses and stationed heavy guards at the End Portal. Some dragons remaining from the war were captured by humans and imprisoned on the Outer Islands of The End. In their later years, these dragons built the 'Inheritance Grounds,' hoping for the rise of future dragon generations. Each year, humanity exiled a batch of death row prisoners to The End to reinforce the seal. As those who went to The End could never return to the Overworld, over the long years, they transformed into Endermen."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&d&lChapter V A New Era"
		"&7        In the new era, conflicts remain common on the Minecraft continent. Dragons dwelling in deep mountains and seas occasionally raid villages, pillaging villagers; some humans have spontaneously formed Dragon Hunter Guilds, dedicating themselves to protecting humanity by hunting dragons. Of course, some dragons have also cultivated deep friendships with humans, leading to the unique profession of Dragon Riders. The bones of fallen dragons from ages past have weathered into Ancient Dragon Dust, Dragon Bones, Dragon Hearts, etc.—excellent magical materials and resources for dragon growth. Scattered across the world are giant dragon statues carved by human slaves for dragons in ancient times, legends say they hide countless treasures, attracting endless adventurers."
		""
		"&6&l【Prologue End】"
	]
	quest.563FC8788BBCE015.quest_subtitle: "Optional Reading"
	quest.563FC8788BBCE015.title: "&bBackstory"
	quest.564CE7EE150DBED0.quest_desc: [
		"&6All cooking processes in Mystia's Izakaya need to be done on a &eStove&r&6. If you want to cook food yourself, a stove is essential~"
		"&6Additionally, you need to craft the cooking utensils corresponding to the dishes. Check the EMI for details.&r&r&r"
	]
